# decision-when-alias-to-reduction root (#189 Slice-C boundary 2, slice 2b.2)
library "Pol".

// A decision whose `when` guard is a `defined as` ALIAS ("Cov Alias") to a reduction ("Cov" =
// `code is` Condition + `exists this`). Post-2b.2 the alias FLIPS at the CQL lane — its Inferred
// define re-exports the reduction's total boolean directly and its Interface façade re-exports
// BARE — so the CQL emit SUCCEEDS. But the underlying is still a reduction whose case-feature SD
// is unconverged, so the FHIR gate must catch it via the guard's TRANSITIVE `defined as` operand
// closure (the direct-reduction gate would MISS the alias, a `DefinedAsDefinition`). Pre-2b.2 the
// alias was blocked transitively by the CQL truth-set THROW; the flip removes that, so the FHIR
// gate re-erects the block.

concept "Cov":
- type is Condition.
- value type is boolean.
- shape is Scalar.
- code is `cov`.
- definition is exists this.

concept "Cov Alias":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- defined as "Cov".

decision "Cov Determination":
first:
- when "Cov Alias" then recommend activity "certify.Approve".
- otherwise then recommend activity "not-certify.Deny".

activity "certify.Approve":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `Coverage determination: APPROVE / Certified.`.
activity "not-certify.Deny":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `Coverage determination: DENY / Not Certified.`.
